    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-054: CSS transform: rotate()**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (four layers, ~110 lines + 4 tests) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## The measurement that shaped this ADR\n\nDiagnostic via `HONEYBEE_LOG=all` with `transform` whitelisted:\n\n```\nTRANSFORM-APPLIED: tag=span class=cdx-text-input__icon\n  cdx-text-input__start-icon prop=transform val=translateY(-50%)\nICON-MEASURE: x=427.50 y=7.00 w=20.00 h=20.00\n(search box: x=418.50 y=7.00 w=256.00 h=42.00)\n```\n\n**Wikipedia uses `translateY(-50%)`, not `rotate()`.** The magnifier needs *both* `top: 50%` and `translateY(-50%)` to center at y=18 in the 42px box — and `top: 50%` requires `parent_content_height` threading (same blocker as ADR-053's `%` max-height). `translateY(-50%)` alone would shift to y=-3 — **above the box**, a regression.\n\nSo this ADR ships **rotate only**, verified via synthetic fixture. Translate deferred.\n\n## What this ADR ships\n\nFour layers, because none exist today:\n\n| Layer | What's missing |\n|---|---|\n| `parse_angle` in style_values | No deg/rad/turn parsing — `parse_length` is pixels only |\n| Whitelist `transform`, `transform-origin` | Parser drops it before cascade |\n| `LayoutBox::transform_rotate_deg` | No field to store it |\n| `cairo_save/rotate/restore` around paint_box | Zero `cairo_rotate` calls in paint.cpp |\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**Wrap the entire `paint_box` body**, not just children or background. CSS `transform` affects rendered pixels — background, border, box-shadow, content, children. Wrapping only part of it would look broken.\n\n**Extract first `rotate()` only**. Other transform functions skipped in v1. `translateY(-50%)` parses to field=0 → zero paint delta → **zero regression** on the magnifier.\n\n**`transform-origin` always 50% 50%** (box center). Custom origins deferred.\n\n**`<img>` transform deferred** — the img early-return path at `layout_element:1721` skips non-img-only post-processing. Documented limitation.\n\n## The new verification category\n\n**Synthetic-fixture verified** — a `data:` URL with `transform:rotate(45deg)` on a red square. Before/after screenshot shows square → diamond, corners at the correct rotated positions. Structurally the same rigor as \"scroll-PNG verified\" but using an inline fixture instead of a scroll position.\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero production PNG delta.** Wikipedia uses `translateY`, not `rotate()`. Rotate parser finds no match → zero paint change → **zero regression** on the search magnifier (primary safety property).\n\n**What ships**: any non-img box with `transform: rotate(Ndeg)` paints rotated by N degrees around its center. First time.\n\n## Test plan\n\n4 new tests:\n1. `parse_angle` unit: 45deg / 0.785rad / 0.125turn / unitless 45\n2. `layout: transform:rotate(45deg)` → `LayoutBox::transform_rotate_deg == 45`\n3. `layout: no transform` → field == 0\n4. `layout: translateY(-50%)` → field == 0 (regression safety)\n\n## Test count\n\n- 647 → 651 cases (after implementation)\n- Documentation only; no code changes yet\n\nRefs #242\n",
